From: HardDinD developers
Subject: [EXPERIMENT] um: retain the physical-memory FD in mapping brokers

Pass a physical-memory FD once per broker instead of sendmsg/recvmsg/close
on every mapping batch. Runners close it before running guest code.
Publish the actual ancillary FD count, skip empty receives, and restore
recvmsg control capacity on each batch with strict truncation checks.

--- a/arch/um/include/shared/skas/mm_id.h
+++ b/arch/um/include/shared/skas/mm_id.h
@@ -19,6 +19,8 @@
 	int sock;
 	int syscall_fd_num;
 	int syscall_fd_map[STUB_MAX_FDS];
+	/* Physical-memory FD retained by a parallel mapping broker at host FD 1. */
+	int cached_phys_fd;
 };
 
 struct mutex *__get_turnstile(struct mm_id *mm_id);
